; HCWBRIDGE on a small plan: floors come from the bridge fixture (HCWBRIDGEIMPORT), the drawing is saved, four walls, a 900 door (D2) and a 1200 window (W3)
; are drawn, and the file next to the drawing is checked: millimetres, a drawing id, the floors with their beam depth, the wall id, the openings with standard marks.
; PREPARE: docs/bridge/fixtures/levels-only.json => levels-only.json
; EXPECT: HCWDOOR: D2/1 900 mm
; EXPECT: HCWWINDOW: W3/1 1200 mm
; EXPECT: HCWBRIDGE: wrote .*export\.aqcbridge\.json
; REJECT: save the drawing first
; REJECT: no floors are defined
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "units":\s*"mm"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "format":\s*"hcw-aqc-bridge"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "drawing_id":\s*"[0-9a-fA-F-]{36}"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "name":\s*"Ground"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "beam_depth_mm":\s*450
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "ref":\s*"W0001"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "thickness_mm":\s*230
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "mark":\s*"D2"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "mark":\s*"W3"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "kind":\s*"Door"
; FILE: export.aqcbridge.json => "width_mm":\s*900
HCWBRIDGEIMPORT
{WORK}\levels-only.json
Y
_.SAVEAS
2018
{WORK}\export.dwg
HCWWALL



0,0
4000,0
4000,3000
0,3000
C

HCWDOOR
D2


2000,100
2000,500

HCWWINDOW
W3


3910,1500

HCWBRIDGE

(princ "\nEXPORT-DONE")
